      { q: "How much should a pest control company spend on marketing?", a: "Industry benchmarks suggest allocating 5 to 10 percent of revenue to marketing. For a pest control company doing one million in annual revenue, that is 50,000 to 100,000 dollars per year across all channels including automation software, advertising, and SEO." },
      { q: "How effective are reactivation campaigns for pest control?", a: "Reactivation campaigns targeting customers who have not booked in 12 or more months typically achieve a 10 to 20 percent response rate. The cost per reactivated customer is 70 to 80 percent lower than acquiring a new customer." },
      { q: "Can marketing automation help sell recurring pest control plans?", a: "Yes. Automated email and SMS sequences educating one-time customers about the benefits of recurring protection, combined with a limited-time enrollment offer, consistently convert 15 to 25 percent of one-time customers to recurring plans." },
      { q: "What seasonal campaigns should a pest control company run?", a: "Essential campaigns include rodent prevention in fall, termite awareness in spring, mosquito and wasp treatment in late spring, and bed bug awareness in late summer. Each campaign should launch 2 to 4 weeks before peak demand for that pest type." }
